======================================================================
3. Individual applications (apps/<app_id>/)
======================================================================

The license of each application is defined by that application. Unless
an application states otherwise, the following applies, as also shown
in the "Information" pane of the portal:

  - Source code generated by AI: no copyright is claimed (equivalent to
    CC0 / public domain, to the extent permitted by law).
  - Parts of the source code modified by a human: licensed under the
    BSD Zero Clause License (0BSD).
  - Prompts and dialogues (the "promptUrl" in meta.json): licensed by
    their author under the license given in "promptLicense" in
    meta.json (for example, CC BY 4.0).
  - Referenced open-source software (the "referencedOSS" in meta.json):
    code that relies on such software remains subject to the license of
    that software, which takes precedence over the terms above.

Third-party libraries bundled in an application (for example, files
under apps/<app_id>/assets/) remain under their respective licenses.
